SYNTHETIC – the window of a trace log that starts inside a <password> element opened before the
window (US1-9): lines 1–2 hold only the value, line 3 the last part of the value, the end tag
</password> and more XML; line 6 holds a complete <password> element (start and end tag).
Expected from SecretTextMasker.maskLines: line 1 is ${secret:data.password}, line 2 is empty,
line 3 equals </password><mode>basic</mode></login>, line 6 is
<login><user>acme</user><password>${secret:data.password}</password></login>, every other line
unchanged; 7 lines in and out; no credential-payload-value-0001 left.
Used by SecretTextMaskerLinesTest (tasks.md T014, research D-11).
